        "original_id": "c671805c-0890-5a80-a711-90f3eb591c26",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Ezhou, Quzhou, Hubei Province, Zhejiang Province, China\n- People: Trần Ích Tắc, Trần Quốc Khang, Trần Thái Tông, Trần Thánh Tông, Trần Quang Khải, Trần Nhật Duật\n- Organizations: Yuan Dynasty\n- Roles: prefecture-level city, King of Annam, prince, emperor\n\nFacts:\n- Ezhou is a prefecture-level city in eastern Hubei Province, China.\n- Quzhou is a prefecture-level city in western Zhejiang Province, People's Republic of China.\n- Trần Quốc Khang, who lived from 1237 to 1300, was Prince Tĩnh Quốc, the first prince of Emperor Trần Thái Tông, and the eldest brother of Trần Thánh Tông, Trần Quang Khải, Trần Ích Tắc, and Trần Nhật Duật.\n- After another failed attempt by the Yuan Dynasty to return Trần Ích Tắc as King of Annam, Trần Ích Tắc continued to live in Ezhou, Hubei, and ultimately died on foreign soil.",
